# Project Rules and Patterns

## Project-Specific Patterns
- This project focuses on monitoring whale/market maker wallets on Ethereum and Arbitrum
- Trading signals are delivered via Telegram bot
- Core functionality revolves around transaction flow analysis
- System follows a modular, event-driven architecture

## Development Preferences
- Python is the primary language for development
- Use clear, descriptive variable names related to blockchain concepts
- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines for Python code
- Document all functions, classes, and complex logic
- Implement proper error handling for API calls and blockchain interactions

## Implementation Guidelines
- Separate concerns between data fetching, analysis, and notification
- Implement proper logging for debugging and monitoring
- Design wallet registry to be easily configurable/extensible
- Prioritize system reliability and near real-time notifications
- Optimize for handling rate limits of blockchain explorer APIs

## File Organization
- Keep blockchain-specific code in separate modules
- Organize code by functional components (fetching, analysis, notification)
- Store configuration in easily modifiable files
- Maintain test files alongside implementation

## Workflow Considerations
- Update Memory Bank regularly as the project evolves
- Document all significant design decisions
- Keep track of added wallet addresses and their significance
- Monitor and document API usage patterns to avoid rate limiting
